  "content": {
    "id": "p2-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "A rectangle of dimensions $x\\text{ cm}\\times y\\text{ cm}$ has a perimeter of $10\\text{ cm}$. If $x$ is increased by $50\\%$ and $y$ is decreased by $50\\%$, then the resulting rectangle has a perimeter of $6\\text{ cm}$. Find $x$ and $y$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=0.5,\\quad y=4.5$; the original dimensions are $0.5\\text{ cm}\\times4.5\\text{ cm}$.\n\nUse the perimeter equations before and after the percentage changes.",
      "worked": "The original perimeter gives\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+2y&=10\\\\x+y&=5\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe new dimensions are $1.5x\\text{ cm}$ and $0.5y\\text{ cm}$, so\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2(1.5x)+2(0.5y)&=6\\\\3x+y&=6\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubtract $x+y=5$ from $3x+y=6$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2x&=1\\\\x&=0.5\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into $x+y=5$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}0.5+y&=5\\\\y&=4.5\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original dimensions are $0.5\\text{ cm}\\times4.5\\text{ cm}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 108
  },
